   "id": "2099705965092159750",
   "url": "https://x.com/DrAlexUrology/status/2099705965092159750",
   "conversationId": "2099705965092159750",
   "text": "If this was an attempt to report without bias, objectively, on an issue that creates a great headache for physicians + patients, this could have been a Pulitzer worthy article. \n\nInstead, the article is nothing but a political hit piece before elections. \n\nIt fails to consider the reality, the physician/practice perspective. Have you considered the alternative? No OB-GYN when you need one?  Very common in many rural counties. \n\nHow do you think medical practices can provide care to the low income patients if they don’t get paid?\n\nEmployees have to be paid.  \nRent has to be paid. \nTaxes have to be paid. \nMalpractice has to be paid. \nSupplies have to be paid for. \n\nDo you have a proposal, a solution?\n\nPhysicians cannot deduct non-collectible debt on tax returns. \nThe government doesn’t pay physicians to take care of the uninsured, and neither does the NYT. \n\nThe article is a mindless political hit on a physician who have given so much to his patients.",
   "lang": "en",
   "createdAt": "2026-09-15T03:44:47.000Z",
   "type": "quote",
   "author": {
